course: dictionary
lesson: 48
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. «Accordion» can name a musical instrument, or it can describe something that folds in zigzags. The words around it tell you which meaning is right.
explain: «The saguaro cactus's pleated stem swells like an accordion to store water.» There is no music in this sentence. The stem has folds, so accordion here describes something folding in zigzags. Test it: put the instrument meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. It does not.
explain: Always ask what the word is doing in the sentence. Is it a thing you could hold, or a word describing how something looks or moves? Accordion can be both, so check the clues before you decide.
fact: An accordion is a musical instrument you hold in your hands and squeeze in and out.
fact: The folding middle part of an accordion pushes air through reeds while you press its keys or buttons.
fact: When accordion comes before a noun, it means folding in zigzags, as in accordion pleats or an accordion file.
fact: «Accordion» can be a noun, as in «an accordion», or it can describe something, as in «accordion folds».
exercise: «She pressed the keys as she squeezed the folding middle part of her accordion.» What is an accordion? | A tall plant that stores water | A bag for carrying books | *A musical instrument you squeeze in and out | A kind of paper fan
exercise: «The saguaro's pleated stem swells like an accordion.» What does accordion mean here? | *Folding in zigzags | A sharp prickle | A loud, cheerful tune | A musical instrument
exercise: «The saguaro's pleated stem swells like an accordion.» Which word in the sentence tells you the stem has folds? | *pleated | accordion | swells | store
test: «The file had accordion pleats, so it opened out in zigzags.» What does accordion mean in accordion pleats? | Very old | Wet and grey | A musical instrument | *Folding in zigzags
test: «Sam heard an accordion playing a French folk tune at the market.» What is an accordion? | A paper toy that cannot be opened | A big folding bag for books | A kind of cactus | *A musical instrument you squeeze in and out
exam: «She kept her notes in an accordion file.» Which meaning of accordion is used here? | A place where folk music is played | A loud, cheerful song | *Folding in zigzags, so the file opens out in folds | A musical instrument you press with your hands
